# =============================================================================
# Customer Churn Prediction — .gitignore
#
# Portfolio-project policy (documented, not default-blind):
#
# 1. DATASET (data/raw/Telco-Customer-Churn.csv) — TRACKED, not ignored.
#    Reasoning: this is the public IBM Telco Customer Churn benchmark
#    (~950 KB, no personal/sensitive data beyond a customerID identifier),
#    already widely mirrored on GitHub. Committing it lets anyone clone the
#    repo and run the notebooks/app immediately, without hunting for the
#    file or guessing which mirror was used. Trade-off: slightly larger
#    repo; acceptable given the file's small size.
#
# 2. TRAINED MODEL (models/churn_model.pkl) — TRACKED, not ignored.
#    Reasoning: the Streamlit app depends on this file to run without
#    retraining. Committing it means a recruiter/reviewer can run
#    `streamlit run app/app.py` right after cloning. Trade-off: binary
#    diffs in git history if retrained; acceptable at ~850 KB for a
#    single-owner portfolio repo. (In a team/production setting this would
#    instead go through a model registry or release asset, not git.)
#
# 3. FIGURES & REPORT TABLES (reports/) — TRACKED, not ignored.
#    These are portfolio evidence (EDA plots, confusion matrices, ROC
#    curves, SHAP plots, CV/test result tables) that the README references
#    directly. A reviewer should see them on GitHub without running any
#    code.
#
# 4. Processed data (data/processed/) is INTENTIONALLY EMPTY and stays
#    that way — see Step 3: no globally-fit transformed dataset is ever
#    saved there, since reusing one for modeling would reintroduce leakage.
#    The folder + .gitkeep are tracked so the project structure is visible.
# =============================================================================

# Byte-compiled / cache
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.pyc

# Virtual environments
venv/
.venv/
env/
ENV/

# Jupyter
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# OS files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# IDE
.vscode/
.idea/

# Streamlit
.streamlit/

# Logs
*.log

# Environment variables / secrets
.env

# Keep data/processed/ empty except for its placeholder (see policy note above)
data/processed/*
!data/processed/.gitkeep
